    {
      "id": "claim_362918db0fca4e57b7ab8061028c5e4d",
      "statement": "The put_cas error contract is load-bearing for the self-fence: Ok(None) is a clean 412/409 rejection, every other failure is ambiguous (the write may have committed) and surfaces as Err; the conditional-write client is built with retries OFF so a retried CAS put cannot land on the first attempt and convert 'may have committed' into a false 412 rejection.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/bucket.rs#L138-L146",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7bee8d3f4501743be339391c0322a6d4301382cd9bd76441d79e3bb64850f333:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/bucket.rs#L22-L27",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d0a1f50f8752d28ac8b5087975ac723e5c1441b13865fe1ce3423d942566663e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_28b5d8392ead41dbbf85a1d387c0f9fa",
      "statement": "Qualified object stores: Amazon S3, Cloudflare R2, Tigris, Google Cloud Storage, and Azure Blob Storage; release tests run against R2 with the S3 path using the same client and headers. Backblaze B2, Hetzner Object Storage, and DigitalOcean Spaces do not implement the conditional writes celld requires — celld is not correct on such a store — and a store that accepts but ignores the conditions fails late and silently, so the storage test must be run.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L40-L49",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e8fe28a6f6f79a7f0e5bad2e959355b3b51fd14053377d2331565b0b335615f3:"
